,"verificationNotes":["The supplied name exactly matches the normalized official Steam name for the supplied App ID."],"research":{"steam":{"status":"success","checkedAt":"2026-10-15T10:22:49.640Z","error":null}},"steamMetadata":{"appId":"373750","links":{"store":"https://store.steampowered.com/app/373750/","officialWebsite":null,"support":null},"storageRequirements":{"kind":"required_free_space","windows":{"minimum":{"value":400,"unit":"MB","display":"400 MB","approximateBytes":400000000,"evidenceText":"Storage: 400 MB"},"recommended":{"value":400,"unit":"MB","display":"400 MB","approximateBytes":400000000,"evidenceText":"Storage: 400 MB"}},"macos":{"minimum":null,"recommended":null},"linux":{"minimum":null,"recommended":null},"note":"Steam publishes required free space, not the exact installed or download size."},"controllerSupport":{"level":"unknown","xboxCompatible":null,"xboxEvidence":null,"note":"Generic Steam controller support does not prove Xbox controller compatibility."},"playerModes":{"singlePlayer":true,"multiplayer":false,"coop":false,"onlineCoop":false,"localCoop":false,"lanCoop":false,"sharedOrSplitScreen":false,"pvp":false,"maximumPlayers":null,"maximumPlayersNote":"The public Steam app-details response does not provide a reliable exact player limit.","evidence":["Single-player"]},"genres":["Action","Indie","RPG","Simulation","Early Access"],"categories":[{"id":2,"description":"Single-player"},{"id":44,"description":"Remote Play Together"},{"id":62,"description":"Family Sharing"}]}},"content":{"status":"success","steamAppId":"373750","steamName":"DinoSystem","sourceUrl":"https://store.steampowered.com/app/373750/","fetchedAt":"2026-10-16T09:06:15.224252+00:00","locales":{"en":{"status":"source","provider":"steam","shortDescription":"A living prehistoric ecosystem that does not revolve around you. Shape the island as a god, or enter it as a human and survive while animals, weather, water, terrain and your own body change over time.","detailedDescription":"ONE ISLAND, TWO WAYS TO PLAY\n\nDinoSystem is a living prehistoric ecosystem where everything is connected.\n\nPlay as a godlike overseer and shape the island from above, or enter the world as a human and try to survive inside it.\n\nIn God Mode, you can observe and manipulate the ecosystem, alter the environment, control animals and experiment with the systems that keep the island alive.\n\nIn Survival Mode, you are just another creature in that world. Find food and water, build shelter, hunt, fish, craft tools and learn how to live alongside the animals around you.\n\nThe island is not built around you. It keeps changing whether you interfere or not.\n\nNOTHING APPEARS JUST BECAUSE THE GAME NEEDS IT\n\nAnimals are born, grow, reproduce, age and die. Plants grow according to environmental conditions. Water flows through the terrain and collects in puddles, rivers and lakes. Weather changes the world around you.\n\nEvery creature needs food, water and shelter. Predators depend on prey. Herbivores depend on vegetation. Populations can grow, migrate, decline or disappear depending on what happens around them.\n\nThere are no scripted encounters designed to keep you entertained.\n\nThe world simply keeps running.\n\nYou can interfere with it, study it, exploit it or simply try to survive inside it.\n\nYOUR BODY IS PART OF THE SIMULATION\n\nSurvival is not just about managing an inventory.\n\nYour body changes according to the way you live.\n\nFood affects your nutrition and body composition. Physical activity affects your stamina and muscle. Temperature, hydration, sleep and exertion all interact with your physical condition.\n\nEat too much and you can gain weight.\n\nWork hard and your body adapts.\n\nStay cold, hungry, dehydrated or exhausted for too long and your performance suffers.\n\nYour character is not just a collection of statistics. Your physical condition is part of the simulation.\n\nA WORLD OF CONNECTED SYSTEMS\n\nDinoSystem is built around systems that interact with one another rather than existing as isolated features.\n\nWeather affects temperature and water.\n\nWater affects vegetation.\n\nVegetation affects herbivores.\n\nHerbivores affect predators.\n\nYour actions can alter these relationships in ways that are not always predictable.\n\nThe island is procedurally generated, with different terrain, vegetation and water systems creating a different environment each time.\n\nYou can hunt, fish, gather, farm, craft, build and explore, but none of these activities exist in isolation from the world around you.\n\nThere are dinosaurs, mammals, birds, reptiles and other animals, each with their own needs and behaviours.\n\nThere are seasons, changing weather, fires, reproduction, aging, diseases, injuries and many other systems working together beneath the surface.\n\nThe result is a world that can produce situations the game never explicitly planned.\n\nSURVIVE YOUR WAY\n\nThere is no single correct way to play DinoSystem.\n\nYou can build a safe home and live off the land.\n\nYou can become a hunter.\n\nYou can fish, farm or gather.\n\nYou can explore the island and adapt to whatever you find.\n\nOr you can simply observe the ecosystem and see what happens.\n\nIf you want to experiment, God Mode lets you interfere with the world directly.\n\nIf you want to test yourself, Survival Mode puts you inside the simulation with nothing guaranteed.\n\nThe same world powers both experiences.\n\nYou are simply looking at it from a different perspective.\n\nEARLY ACCESS\n\nDinoSystem is a solo-developed project and is still being expanded and refined.\n\nBoth game modes and the core simulation are playable now. Late-game variety and the remaining God Mode tools are still being improved on the road to version 1.0.\n\n⚠️ WARNING: The Remote Play Together tag is used solely to enable multi-device play and does not indicate any multiplayer functionality.","aboutGame":null},"vi":{"status":"pending_translation","provider":nul